1
00:00:05,701 --> 00:00:07,143
(All characters, places, and organizations
in this drama are fictitious.)

2
00:00:07,168 --> 00:00:08,763
(Filming followed broadcast guidelines
for minors, some scenes used AI.)

3
00:00:11,143 --> 00:00:13,220
Gyu Rim might have eaten them.

4
00:00:14,137 --> 00:00:17,015
What if she did eat them?

5
00:00:23,801 --> 00:00:25,087
Mu Jin!

6
00:00:26,749 --> 00:00:29,405
Did you eat the oysters...

7
00:00:29,430 --> 00:00:32,070
Oysters? What oysters?

8
00:00:32,095 --> 00:00:35,187
- Did you eat them?
- Are you asking if I ate them?

9
00:00:37,392 --> 00:00:39,473
Su Nam...

10
00:00:39,498 --> 00:00:41,524
The oysters Su Nam brought over?

11
00:00:41,644 --> 00:00:44,770
I didn't eat them. They're in the fridge.
I'll make oyster pancakes for the kids.

12
00:00:46,254 --> 00:00:50,331
Mu Jin, what's going on?

13
00:00:50,432 --> 00:00:52,217
You ran all the way
here instead of driving?

14
00:00:52,242 --> 00:00:55,812
Some jerk had me blocked in,
so I couldn't get my car out.

15
00:00:55,837 --> 00:00:58,923
Some jerk blocked your car?

16
00:00:59,750 --> 00:01:01,867
You ran all the way here
from the restaurant?

17
00:01:01,892 --> 00:01:03,798
You should've just called.

18
00:01:03,897 --> 00:01:07,374
You didn't pick up.

19
00:01:07,423 --> 00:01:09,261
I didn't pick up?

20
00:01:12,530 --> 00:01:14,237
I left my phone at the shop.

21
00:01:17,743 --> 00:01:21,055
I'm sorry. Get up.

22
00:01:21,080 --> 00:01:23,420
Let's go home and at least
get you some water.

23
00:01:23,445 --> 00:01:24,876
Look at you.

24
00:01:27,129 --> 00:01:28,834
What happened to you?

25
00:01:28,859 --> 00:01:31,988
Why were you stumbling around out there?

26
00:01:32,129 --> 00:01:35,799
Something I ate at lunch didn't sit well,
so I felt a little dizzy.

27
00:01:37,346 --> 00:01:39,288
Did you take some medicine?

28
00:01:39,374 --> 00:01:41,608
Yeah, I did. I'm fine now.

29
00:01:41,633 --> 00:01:43,131
Thank goodness.

30
00:01:43,371 --> 00:01:46,024
I was so scared you'd eaten the oysters,

31
00:01:47,819 --> 00:01:50,423
that something had happened to you.

32
00:01:55,210 --> 00:01:57,059
Is something wrong with the oysters?

33
00:01:57,857 --> 00:02:00,813
No, it's nothing.
Good thing you didn't eat them.

34
00:02:00,957 --> 00:02:03,026
Make sure you throw them out later.

35
00:02:04,317 --> 00:02:07,437
You ran all the way here from work
just to stop me from eating oysters.

36
00:02:07,696 --> 00:02:10,410
How can you love me this much?

37
00:02:11,877 --> 00:02:13,917
I can't even give back a quarter of that.

38
00:02:14,156 --> 00:02:16,888
You have a lot of people to take care of.

39
00:02:18,036 --> 00:02:22,352
In this life, love me as much as you can,

40
00:02:22,573 --> 00:02:27,606
and whatever love you can't give me,
just carry it over into the next life.

41
00:02:30,075 --> 00:02:32,535
Why aren't you answering? Stop smiling.

42
00:02:33,009 --> 00:02:34,580
You don't want to meet in the next life?

43
00:02:34,757 --> 00:02:37,813
No. Let's meet in the next life too.

44
00:02:38,877 --> 00:02:40,917
But next time, be born as my son, Mu Jin.

45
00:02:41,564 --> 00:02:44,468
So I can just give you love
instead of getting it.

46
00:02:45,044 --> 00:02:47,138
So I can just pour it all on you.

47
00:02:51,984 --> 00:02:54,064
I'm so relieved.

48
00:02:54,270 --> 00:02:56,786
- Look at you sweat.
- I'm just glad you're okay.

49
00:02:57,173 --> 00:03:00,093
(Hui Na)

50
00:03:07,123 --> 00:03:10,523
The person you are calling is unavailable.
You will be connected to voicemail...

51
00:03:17,364 --> 00:03:19,053
This is Seo Min Ju's doing.

52
00:03:21,230 --> 00:03:24,286
I know the slang she uses online,
the way she talks, her tone, everything.

53
00:03:24,337 --> 00:03:26,033
She posted it. A hundred percent.

54
00:03:26,644 --> 00:03:30,191
She kept pestering Yun Gi and me
to tell her where you were.

55
00:03:30,784 --> 00:03:33,448
She said it wasn't her,
but her mom who was looking for you.

56
00:03:35,997 --> 00:03:40,890
Hey, that woman you used to hustle...

57
00:03:42,597 --> 00:03:44,223
She wasn't Min Ju's mom, was she?

58
00:03:52,137 --> 00:03:54,108
Seriously, are you out of your mind?

59
00:03:55,022 --> 00:03:57,188
How can you marry a gigolo?

60
00:03:58,296 --> 00:04:01,827
He's not a gigolo. Not anymore.

61
00:04:03,031 --> 00:04:05,724
Why are you being such an idiot?

62
00:04:07,071 --> 00:04:10,752
So you kill someone, then claim innocence
because you won't kill anymore?

63
00:04:10,830 --> 00:04:13,239
I heard the principal called you in
and warned you,

64
00:04:13,390 --> 00:04:15,447
asking what you'd do if the rumor
spread further at school,

65
00:04:15,744 --> 00:04:17,637
what you'd do
if the parents started protesting.

66
00:04:17,764 --> 00:04:20,757
And he pressured you to decide
about your future before that happens.

67
00:04:21,156 --> 00:04:22,947
Anyway, I can't break up with Gyu O.

68
00:04:23,563 --> 00:04:26,524
We even exchanged vows
in front of my grandparents' photo.

69
00:04:27,764 --> 00:04:30,729
So you don't care if you get fired?

70
00:04:31,083 --> 00:04:32,950
You don't care if you lose your paycheck?

71
00:04:32,975 --> 00:04:35,378
Can they just fire someone
because of my husband's past job?

72
00:04:35,476 --> 00:04:37,245
Can they just take away my job?

73
00:04:37,503 --> 00:04:40,867
Guilt by association is long gone.
Can they really do that in a democracy?

74
00:04:41,977 --> 00:04:45,145
Are you selling cabbages?
Baking fish-shaped pastries?

75
00:04:45,544 --> 00:04:49,425
You're a teacher
who teaches young kids, you silly girl.

76
00:04:49,537 --> 00:04:54,302
Don't you know how conservative
and strict the education world is?

77
00:04:54,327 --> 00:04:56,470
If I get fired, I can sell cabbages.

78
00:04:56,857 --> 00:04:58,398
I can make fish-shaped pastries
for a living.

79
00:04:58,603 --> 00:05:02,528
Seriously. If no one were around,
I'd smack you, I swear.

80
00:05:04,510 --> 00:05:06,587
Then what about your parents?

81
00:05:07,070 --> 00:05:08,493
What about Hui Seop?

82
00:05:08,883 --> 00:05:12,128
What about your family?
They live off your salary.

83
00:05:16,025 --> 00:05:17,324
(Shocking, Geumje-dong Elementary Teacher
Kwon Living with Ex-Host Bar Escort?)

84
00:05:17,356 --> 00:05:20,496
A teacher named Kwon
at an elementary school in Geumje-dong...

85
00:05:20,936 --> 00:05:25,096
is living with a gigolo she'll marry,
and that's Gyu O?

86
00:05:28,170 --> 00:05:30,159
Gyu O isn't a gigolo anymore.

87
00:05:30,184 --> 00:05:33,002
And what do you mean, living together?
He sleeps in this room with you every day.

88
00:05:33,750 --> 00:05:35,219
What do we do about Gyu O?

89
00:05:42,711 --> 00:05:45,043
Gyu O's name is in the comments here.

90
00:05:45,583 --> 00:05:50,637
"I was passing by and saw a young woman
and an older woman fight over a man."

91
00:05:51,944 --> 00:05:54,897
"They said the gigolo's name
was Han Gyu O."

92
00:05:56,650 --> 00:05:58,130
"Where's Han Gyu O?"

93
00:05:58,155 --> 00:06:01,116
"The old lady was looking for you.
Come out, Han Gyu O."

94
00:06:01,237 --> 00:06:03,503
This is driving me crazy. Seriously.

95
00:06:04,210 --> 00:06:08,423
No way. It's not him, Gyu Seo.
It's not our Gyu O.

96
00:06:08,870 --> 00:06:12,858
Do you know how many people
are named Han Gyu O? How many gigolos...

97
00:06:14,247 --> 00:06:19,920
You think he's the only gigolo
named Han Gyu O?

98
00:06:20,065 --> 00:06:24,027
People like that almost always use
fake names. In the movies, you know?

99
00:06:24,277 --> 00:06:25,917
It's not him.

100
00:06:33,096 --> 00:06:36,058
What's this? Are you crying?

101
00:06:37,190 --> 00:06:38,515
I'm not crying.

102
00:06:39,290 --> 00:06:42,139
Do you cry every day? Look.

103
00:06:44,927 --> 00:06:47,480
- Tickle.
- Dad!

104
00:06:47,793 --> 00:06:51,366
See? You're crying.
And you're supposed to be a man.

105
00:06:51,391 --> 00:06:54,507
Why do you keep crying out of nowhere?
Are you depressed?

106
00:06:54,532 --> 00:06:55,822
I said I wasn't crying.

107
00:06:55,864 --> 00:06:58,049
Then what's this, rainwater?

108
00:07:02,870 --> 00:07:04,985
- It's because of Gyu O.
- Han Gyu Min!

109
00:07:05,010 --> 00:07:07,598
Dad should know too.
It's about his own son.

110
00:07:08,450 --> 00:07:13,344
Gyu Seo's all torn up over Gyu O.

111
00:07:14,517 --> 00:07:18,313
What's wrong with Gyu O?

112
00:07:18,724 --> 00:07:22,392
My eldest is doing just fine
running a clothing store.

113
00:07:22,417 --> 00:07:23,709
That's the thing...

114
00:07:24,449 --> 00:07:26,717
He's finally doing well.

115
00:07:27,377 --> 00:07:31,622
He's finally trying to live right.

116
00:07:31,977 --> 00:07:35,223
He's trying to live right, and what? What?

117
00:07:35,248 --> 00:07:37,545
Who did what?

118
00:07:37,570 --> 00:07:41,387
Did someone ruin Gyu O's future?

119
00:07:41,412 --> 00:07:44,003
Forget it. Just pretend you don't know.

120
00:07:44,028 --> 00:07:46,816
- How?
- Gyu Rim must never find out.

121
00:07:47,070 --> 00:07:49,260
Gyu Rim can never know.

122
00:07:49,510 --> 00:07:51,994
Gyu Rim? She can't know?

123
00:07:55,184 --> 00:07:56,799
Gyeol went to bed early today.

124
00:07:56,824 --> 00:07:58,210
Did he eat before he went to bed?

125
00:08:03,010 --> 00:08:04,457
Is something wrong?

126
00:08:09,490 --> 00:08:10,803
What is it?

127
00:08:12,445 --> 00:08:13,585
I don't know.

128
00:08:14,765 --> 00:08:18,557
Something's going on with Gyu O, I think.

129
00:08:18,677 --> 00:08:23,850
The twins are crying and making a fuss,
and leaving me out, saying I'll tell you.

130
00:08:27,504 --> 00:08:30,268
What's going on? What about Gyu O?

131
00:08:30,904 --> 00:08:32,718
Did something happen to him?

132
00:08:33,510 --> 00:08:35,433
What did Dad say this time?

133
00:08:36,964 --> 00:08:39,216
What happened to Gyu O?

134
00:08:39,457 --> 00:08:43,343
What on earth happened
that you're all hiding it from me?

135
00:08:44,364 --> 00:08:45,850
Let's just tell her.

136
00:08:45,950 --> 00:08:48,903
It involves Gyeol's homeroom teacher,
so she'll find out anyway.

137
00:08:49,723 --> 00:08:52,250
Gyeol's homeroom teacher? Ms. Kwon?

138
00:08:52,712 --> 00:08:56,076
What about Ms. Kwon?
Did something happen to her?

139
00:09:02,923 --> 00:09:05,511
Gyu Seo. Gyu Min.

140
00:09:08,570 --> 00:09:09,879
I'm not some outsider.

141
00:09:10,357 --> 00:09:13,799
I'm Gyu O's sister. I'm family.

142
00:09:23,177 --> 00:09:27,365
Gyu Rim, even if you hear
something strange about Gyu O,

143
00:09:27,390 --> 00:09:29,459
don't misjudge him or be disappointed.

144
00:09:29,610 --> 00:09:34,313
He's a thousand times more sensitive
and conscientious than Gyu Seo...

145
00:09:34,338 --> 00:09:37,533
Gyu Min, if you put it like that,
I won't understand.

146
00:09:37,863 --> 00:09:43,515
I'm not very bright, so I don't get it.
Explain it more simply.

147
00:09:47,817 --> 00:09:51,514
Gyu O was dating Gyeol's homeroom teacher,

148
00:09:52,308 --> 00:09:56,841
and I don't know if they got married
or if they're planning to,

149
00:09:56,990 --> 00:09:59,702
but someone's been digging up
his personal info online,

150
00:09:59,956 --> 00:10:03,989
putting a target on him,
spreading lies, framing him.

151
00:10:07,577 --> 00:10:09,244
What personal info?

152
00:10:11,217 --> 00:10:12,884
What about his personal info?

153
00:10:15,229 --> 00:10:17,770
What has Gyu O been doing with his life?

154
00:10:26,412 --> 00:10:30,602
Han Gyu O? What are you doing here?

155
00:10:39,854 --> 00:10:42,437
Why? What's wrong?

156
00:10:49,312 --> 00:10:50,645
I came because I'm scared.

157
00:10:54,854 --> 00:10:56,895
I feel like I could do anything...

158
00:10:58,562 --> 00:11:00,479
Like I could kill someone...

159
00:11:03,145 --> 00:11:04,604
I came because I'm scared.

160
00:11:06,395 --> 00:11:07,479
So...

161
00:11:09,895 --> 00:11:13,895
You came here so I'd stop you?

162
00:11:30,312 --> 00:11:33,104
I should've just jumped
back then and died.

163
00:11:33,971 --> 00:11:37,471
Gigolo or not, at least I wouldn't
have to see this mess.

164
00:11:38,687 --> 00:11:41,562
I should've just jumped back then...

165
00:11:42,562 --> 00:11:47,020
Gyu Seo, Gyu Min,
even Dad knew, and I'm the only one...

166
00:11:48,662 --> 00:11:50,953
I was the only one who didn't know.

167
00:11:53,625 --> 00:11:59,625
The kids banded together,
saying you must never find out...

168
00:12:03,395 --> 00:12:05,437
What you don't know can't hurt you.

169
00:12:07,979 --> 00:12:12,979
The kids spared you.
And dumped all the misery on me.

170
00:12:43,479 --> 00:12:45,104
Gyu Rim must know
everything by now, right?

171
00:12:50,604 --> 00:12:55,979
It's all over now. It's all over for me.

172
00:12:59,604 --> 00:13:03,854
So it's all over if Gyu Rim finds out?

173
00:13:04,270 --> 00:13:05,812
She just can't find out.

174
00:13:07,562 --> 00:13:11,395
As long as she doesn't know, I can laugh,
joke around, act tough, act fine,

175
00:13:11,895 --> 00:13:17,229
act like nothing's wrong,
and live as shamelessly as I want...

176
00:13:25,229 --> 00:13:26,395
Right.

177
00:13:27,645 --> 00:13:33,229
It would've been perfect
if she'd never found out...

178
00:13:37,854 --> 00:13:39,270
But you're family. What's the big deal?

179
00:13:44,479 --> 00:13:49,270
If you're ashamed, be ashamed.
If you're embarrassed, be embarrassed.

180
00:13:50,198 --> 00:13:51,698
It's okay to show her all of it.

181
00:13:52,479 --> 00:13:56,645
Because she's family. She's your sister.

182
00:13:58,687 --> 00:14:03,979
Seeing her hurt and struggle will hurt you
far more than your own pain does,

183
00:14:06,062 --> 00:14:09,770
but what can you do?
That's what family is.

184
00:14:11,354 --> 00:14:15,354
It hurts that much more
because you love her that much.

185
00:14:23,892 --> 00:14:28,225
And sure,
the people posting stuff online...

186
00:14:29,145 --> 00:14:32,770
The guys out to stomp on your life
aren't right in the head,

187
00:14:35,604 --> 00:14:41,479
but you have to pay some price too
for the path you took.

188
00:14:44,395 --> 00:14:46,145
That's what makes the world fair.

189
00:14:51,187 --> 00:14:55,395
So don't blame anyone,

190
00:14:59,729 --> 00:15:03,770
and you've already beaten
yourself up enough.

191
00:15:03,906 --> 00:15:08,322
So let's just change
our destination a little.

192
00:15:10,145 --> 00:15:15,729
Our original destination was for Gyu Rim
to never get hurt or cry again.

193
00:15:16,395 --> 00:15:20,729
She might cry from now on,
and she might get hurt,

194
00:15:23,020 --> 00:15:28,645
but whatever tears or hurt come her way,
let's make her twice as happy.

195
00:15:32,145 --> 00:15:36,229
That's the last change to our destination.
No more changes after this.

196
00:15:51,979 --> 00:15:53,645
A lot happened.

197
00:15:55,145 --> 00:15:57,104
It's a long story.

198
00:15:58,321 --> 00:16:01,530
I'm dead tired right now.
Too tired to say a single word.

199
00:16:01,669 --> 00:16:06,363
Can't I answer you some other time,
like at your 100th birthday party?

200
00:16:08,488 --> 00:16:11,146
Aren't you going to congratulate me?

201
00:16:13,406 --> 00:16:18,992
Right. Congratulations, Gyu O.
I'm happy for you.

202
00:16:20,285 --> 00:16:25,785
You have to take care of Ms. Kwon
no matter what and make her happy, okay?

203
00:16:26,479 --> 00:16:29,312
Of course. That's why I'm marrying her.

204
00:16:50,729 --> 00:16:53,145
(Missed Call, Gyu O)

205
00:16:55,604 --> 00:16:57,389
(Gyu O)

206
00:16:57,414 --> 00:16:58,664
(Hui Na! Where are you? Are you okay?
Hui Na, please pick up.)

207
00:16:58,689 --> 00:16:59,689
(Kwon Hui Na, I'm worried,
so call me when you see this.)

208
00:16:59,714 --> 00:17:00,714
(If you don't want to hear my voice,
just send me a dot.)

209
00:17:00,739 --> 00:17:01,739
(I'm going crazy with worry, so please...)

210
00:17:10,562 --> 00:17:12,562
(Mom)

211
00:17:28,062 --> 00:17:32,062
Mom, what are you talking about?
What's wrong with Hui Seop?

212
00:17:35,520 --> 00:17:36,854
Put Hui Seop on.

213
00:17:39,645 --> 00:17:43,145
Hui Seop,
why are you doing this? Seriously!

214
00:17:47,199 --> 00:17:49,729
What do you mean you'll die?

215
00:17:53,520 --> 00:17:56,937
Why do you keep saying
such pathetic things?

216
00:17:58,479 --> 00:18:02,312
Hui Seop, I'll get you better.

217
00:18:03,488 --> 00:18:08,071
I'll search the whole world, the States,
wherever, and get you better.

218
00:18:10,729 --> 00:18:14,562
Yes, I have lots of money.

219
00:18:15,455 --> 00:18:20,288
I've saved up a lot,
and my salary's gone up a lot too.

220
00:18:20,897 --> 00:18:24,564
I've got money coming out of my ears,
so don't worry about money.

221
00:18:28,260 --> 00:18:33,051
What? Please!

222
00:18:37,062 --> 00:18:39,562
Why are you doing this? Seriously!

223
00:18:50,478 --> 00:18:51,565
(Kwon Hui Na, I'm worried,
so call me when you see this.)

224
00:18:51,590 --> 00:18:52,711
(If you don't want to hear my voice,
just send me a dot.)

225
00:18:52,736 --> 00:18:53,862
(I'm going crazy with worry, so please...)

226
00:20:18,395 --> 00:20:19,979
Please don't hurt, Gyu Rim.

227
00:20:24,854 --> 00:20:26,395
Even if it hurts, just a little,

228
00:20:29,145 --> 00:20:30,812
only as much as you can bear.

229
00:20:35,354 --> 00:20:40,604
Please, only as much as you can bear.

230
00:21:24,437 --> 00:21:25,479
Gyu Rim.

231
00:21:29,187 --> 00:21:31,062
Looks like Gyu O came home.

232
00:21:31,510 --> 00:21:34,843
I went to check just in case,
and his shoes are by the door.

233
00:21:35,983 --> 00:21:37,108
Yeah.

234
00:21:38,937 --> 00:21:40,687
You already knew.

235
00:21:44,610 --> 00:21:46,555
You didn't sleep a wink, did you?

236
00:21:47,329 --> 00:21:49,336
I didn't even get three hours of sleep...

237
00:21:49,562 --> 00:21:52,854
And Gyu Seo texted me at 3:30 a.m.
saying he couldn't sleep.

238
00:21:56,187 --> 00:21:59,479
I bet Dad's the only one who slept well.
Just Dad.

239
00:22:17,937 --> 00:22:18,979
Gyu O.

240
00:22:21,645 --> 00:22:23,812
I know you're not asleep, so just get up.

241
00:22:25,312 --> 00:22:26,584
Isn't it stuffy in there?

242
00:22:26,897 --> 00:22:29,171
You've been pretending to sleep
for over an hour and a half.

243
00:22:33,509 --> 00:22:35,562
You're uncanny, you brat.

244
00:22:39,979 --> 00:22:41,604
Were you with Ms. Kwon?

245
00:22:46,395 --> 00:22:49,895
Did you cry all night?
Did I die or something?

246
00:22:50,979 --> 00:22:54,604
No, my pink eye came back, so what?

247
00:22:54,808 --> 00:22:57,017
I'm still alive and kicking.

248
00:22:57,300 --> 00:23:02,050
I don't fall apart over stuff like this,
and I sure don't cry like a baby.

249
00:23:03,312 --> 00:23:07,812
If anything,
it's because the world is fair.

250
00:23:08,770 --> 00:23:09,979
What do you mean?

251
00:23:10,104 --> 00:23:13,437
What goes around comes around.
You reap what you sow.

252
00:23:13,979 --> 00:23:16,645
You do wrong, you pay for it.
You think you just get a pass?

253
00:23:17,229 --> 00:23:19,020
You think fate is that careless?

254
00:23:19,520 --> 00:23:20,562
Gyu O.

255
00:23:23,062 --> 00:23:26,354
I'm hungry. I'm making ramen. Want some?

256
00:23:28,145 --> 00:23:29,187
Come on out.

257
00:23:29,687 --> 00:23:32,895
I put away everything I could,
brooms, baseball bats, all of it,

258
00:23:33,020 --> 00:23:35,812
so no matter what he says,
don't hit him, Gyu Rim.

259
00:23:35,979 --> 00:23:38,104
I swear, I can vouch for our Gyu O...

260
00:23:38,104 --> 00:23:39,520
Your Gyu O what?

261
00:23:43,562 --> 00:23:45,479
It's not your Gyu O that's the problem...

262
00:23:46,520 --> 00:23:49,479
Hey, is that any face for a lady?

263
00:23:51,520 --> 00:23:53,270
You've got so much gunk in your eyes, kid.

264
00:23:55,597 --> 00:23:56,854
Is there any leftover rice, Gyu Rim?

265
00:23:57,562 --> 00:23:59,653
I want to dump some in my ramen.

266
00:24:00,812 --> 00:24:04,979
Let's see. No ramen? None?

267
00:24:05,645 --> 00:24:07,645
Did Dad already eat it all?

268
00:24:10,604 --> 00:24:14,187
Why don't we make ginseng chicken soup?

269
00:24:16,520 --> 00:24:19,104
There was exactly one abalone
in the freezer,

270
00:24:19,145 --> 00:24:21,645
and the lucky one just might find it.

271
00:24:23,979 --> 00:24:27,020
Line up over here
if you want ginseng chicken soup.

272
00:24:29,520 --> 00:24:33,770
Nobody wants chicken soup?
First come, first served. Only three.

273
00:24:40,979 --> 00:24:43,520
You're not lining up?
She said the first three.

274
00:24:43,845 --> 00:24:44,886
What?

275
00:24:45,145 --> 00:24:48,979
Gyu Min, you're not having any?
Don't you know my soup is to die for?

276
00:24:52,312 --> 00:24:54,979
I know. I totally know.

277
00:24:55,937 --> 00:24:58,312
I'm in too. First three.

278
00:25:12,895 --> 00:25:15,479
My poor Gyu O.

279
00:25:19,145 --> 00:25:22,395
I thought he was finally
living a decent life...

280
00:25:25,145 --> 00:25:28,312
What do I do? My poor eldest son...

281
00:25:28,645 --> 00:25:32,562
Now's not the time, Dad. Get up.

282
00:25:48,604 --> 00:25:50,354
You're only making three servings?

283
00:25:50,812 --> 00:25:54,520
Our family goes nuts over chicken soup.
Won't there be a war?

284
00:25:55,937 --> 00:25:58,479
Right, there's going to be a war?

285
00:26:00,020 --> 00:26:03,604
Then could you hurry
and buy two more chickens?

286
00:26:04,312 --> 00:26:06,312
Yeah, okay.

287
00:26:32,770 --> 00:26:34,437
Everyone's pretending?

288
00:26:34,562 --> 00:26:39,020
Yeah. Pretending they're fine,
pretending nothing happened,

289
00:26:40,229 --> 00:26:41,895
pretending nothing ever happened at all.

290
00:26:42,520 --> 00:26:43,604
Why?

291
00:26:43,729 --> 00:26:46,145
Because they don't want to face the pain.

292
00:26:46,187 --> 00:26:50,395
So they overdo it, change the subject,
and avoid each other.

293
00:26:50,645 --> 00:26:51,687
Why?

294
00:26:51,729 --> 00:26:52,770
"Why?"

295
00:26:53,770 --> 00:26:57,145
So you'd rather Gyu O scowl
and say, "I'm in pain,"

296
00:26:57,187 --> 00:26:58,895
and avoid running into the family,

297
00:26:59,145 --> 00:27:02,312
and Gyu Rim broadcast her pain
to the whole neighborhood like you do,

298
00:27:02,354 --> 00:27:04,770
bawling her eyes out? As grown adults?

299
00:27:07,895 --> 00:27:09,687
You're taking a dig at me, aren't you?

300
00:27:10,604 --> 00:27:14,187
So act like an adult too, Dad.

301
00:27:14,212 --> 00:27:17,087
Don't show all your feelings like a child.

302
00:27:18,354 --> 00:27:22,520
How Gyu Rim and Gyu O came
from a dad like you...

303
00:27:22,687 --> 00:27:25,229
is the biggest mystery of my life.

304
00:27:25,395 --> 00:27:28,062
Gyu Seo's quiet, so now it's your turn?

305
00:27:28,187 --> 00:27:32,395
You keep ganging up on me.
Gyu Rim, Gyu O, you twins,

306
00:27:32,437 --> 00:27:35,656
do you think a single one of you
is normal?

307
00:27:35,770 --> 00:27:38,020
Do you think there's even one of you
I can brag about...

308
00:27:38,104 --> 00:27:40,812
at class reunions like my friends do?

309
00:27:41,895 --> 00:27:47,020
I'm so frustrated. Anyway,
at least read the room.

310
00:27:47,104 --> 00:27:49,770
Even if you're a bad actor, just act.

311
00:27:50,933 --> 00:27:52,350
You're so frustrating.

312
00:28:03,604 --> 00:28:10,229
A bunch of chickens were at a crosswalk,
and the light turned green.

313
00:28:10,687 --> 00:28:14,562
What did the chicken in front say?

314
00:28:17,562 --> 00:28:19,145
"Chicken run!"

315
00:28:22,812 --> 00:28:29,729
Hey, it's funny, right? Hey, it's funny.
"Chicken run!" Funny, right?

316
00:28:46,562 --> 00:28:52,687
A chicken was walking down the street
and fell down.

317
00:28:54,520 --> 00:28:55,562
What did it say?

318
00:28:57,562 --> 00:28:58,604
"Fowl down!"

319
00:29:03,922 --> 00:29:05,395
Hey, that's funny!

320
00:29:08,854 --> 00:29:11,812
Hey, if it's funny, laugh.
Don't hold it in.

321
00:29:15,562 --> 00:29:17,520
Funny, right? "Fowl down."

322
00:29:19,770 --> 00:29:23,020
Dad, I hung my laundry up on the roof,

323
00:29:23,145 --> 00:29:25,604
and I forgot my underwear up there.
Come get it with me.

324
00:29:25,729 --> 00:29:27,562
All of a sudden,
while I'm eating a drumstick?

325
00:29:27,587 --> 00:29:29,212
Eat when we get back.

326
00:29:29,283 --> 00:29:32,924
Hey, what's with the underwear
all of a sudden?

327
00:29:32,949 --> 00:29:35,498
If you've got nothing to wear,
just wear Gyu O's.

328
00:29:35,895 --> 00:29:36,895
Why would I wear his?

329
00:29:36,937 --> 00:29:39,354
- Hey, my drumstick!
- Hurry.

330
00:29:40,582 --> 00:29:43,862
Mom, why is the mood
at home so weird today?

331
00:29:46,776 --> 00:29:49,964
What's weird? It's not weird at all.

332
00:29:51,196 --> 00:29:54,063
- Gyeol, have some broth too.
- Okay.

333
00:29:59,203 --> 00:30:00,630
"Chicken run" isn't funny?

334
00:30:02,497 --> 00:30:04,090
"Fowl down" really isn't funny?

335
00:30:15,417 --> 00:30:17,594
- Come out here.
- Why?

336
00:30:17,637 --> 00:30:19,643
- I was eating!
- It's not funny.

337
00:30:19,668 --> 00:30:21,444
What's so funny?

338
00:30:22,197 --> 00:30:24,216
Why do you keep cracking weird dad jokes
that make Gyu O uncomfortable?

339
00:30:24,364 --> 00:30:25,957
What's gotten into you?

340
00:30:26,909 --> 00:30:29,724
You guys said I should!

341
00:30:29,824 --> 00:30:33,018
You said to go over the top and make jokes
so he can't think about anything!

342
00:30:33,043 --> 00:30:34,890
Can't you just stay out of it?

343
00:30:35,877 --> 00:30:40,037
Would it kill you to just be the grown-up
and quietly have his back?

344
00:30:43,363 --> 00:30:46,658
You nag me when I cry,
you nag me when I crack jokes.

345
00:30:46,836 --> 00:30:48,923
Which tune am I supposed to dance to?

346
00:30:48,924 --> 00:30:50,978
Then don't dance. Just sit tight.

347
00:31:25,510 --> 00:31:26,704
"Chicken run."

348
00:31:27,350 --> 00:31:28,513
"Fowl down."

349
00:31:31,721 --> 00:31:34,824
I'm tearing up.

350
00:31:46,616 --> 00:31:48,454
Do you have this in a bigger size?

351
00:31:51,684 --> 00:31:53,357
Yes, we do.

352
00:31:56,530 --> 00:31:57,613
Han Gyu O.

353
00:31:58,819 --> 00:32:00,957
We do have a bigger size, ma'am.

354
00:32:01,557 --> 00:32:04,520
But I think the one you're holding
should fit you just fine,

355
00:32:04,545 --> 00:32:06,726
- so why don't you try it on first?
- Sure.

356
00:32:06,942 --> 00:32:09,088
- I'll show you this way.
- Okay.

357
00:32:16,763 --> 00:32:18,686
What? Why are you here?

358
00:32:20,023 --> 00:32:21,357
Gotta make a living. Why?

359
00:32:21,610 --> 00:32:22,804
No, that's not what I mean.

360
00:32:22,890 --> 00:32:26,029
I'll sort the boxes that came in,
so help the customer when she comes out.

361
00:32:27,683 --> 00:32:28,683
What about Hui Na?

362
00:32:29,346 --> 00:32:30,531
Have you heard from her?

363
00:32:31,765 --> 00:32:32,765
Did you see her?

364
00:32:37,996 --> 00:32:39,914
You've been stabbed in the back
more than once lately.

365
00:32:40,024 --> 00:32:42,506
Why are you so shocked all of a sudden?

366
00:32:44,827 --> 00:32:47,022
- Are you sure?
- I'm sure.

367
00:32:47,823 --> 00:32:50,745
I even went all the way down
to Geumyeong Bay just in case.

368
00:32:51,744 --> 00:32:56,460
The second I looked Mr. Im in the eye,
I had a hunch.

369
00:32:56,611 --> 00:33:00,388
This jerk's hiding something.
It wasn't just a mistake.

370
00:33:02,643 --> 00:33:07,115
I sat with Mr. Im all night,
coaxing him, reasoning with him,

371
00:33:07,567 --> 00:33:12,411
even threatening to blacklist him,
and he finally spilled it.

372
00:33:13,183 --> 00:33:15,150
He said he got a call from Seo Yong Cheol.

373
00:33:15,796 --> 00:33:20,144
That he lost his mind
when he was offered a big payout.

374
00:33:22,896 --> 00:33:24,376
Where's Yong Cheol now?

375
00:33:24,830 --> 00:33:27,009
In hiding. His phone's off too.

376
00:33:31,978 --> 00:33:33,210
Who could it be?

377
00:33:35,003 --> 00:33:36,749
Who would go this far against me?

378
00:33:37,657 --> 00:33:39,924
What grudge could they have against me?

379
00:33:40,016 --> 00:33:41,016
Me?

380
00:33:41,777 --> 00:33:45,016
- You're crazy.
- You never know. It could be me.

381
00:33:45,904 --> 00:33:47,444
Judging by how relentless they are,

382
00:33:47,445 --> 00:33:52,460
there's a 99 percent chance it's someone
very close to you with a stake in this.

383
00:33:53,342 --> 00:33:56,368
From now on, don't trust me.
Don't trust anyone.

384
00:33:56,774 --> 00:33:57,905
Trust your family,

385
00:34:00,042 --> 00:34:01,416
your own blood and no one else.

386
00:34:25,842 --> 00:34:27,457
- Jeong Woo.
- Yeah?

387
00:34:29,823 --> 00:34:33,818
If you ever find out
who's behind all this...

388
00:34:33,843 --> 00:34:36,140
They should get the maximum sentence.

389
00:34:36,519 --> 00:34:37,744
Don't tell me.

390
00:34:38,110 --> 00:34:40,923
Why? Afraid you'll go shoot them yourself?

391
00:34:41,017 --> 00:34:44,588
Keep it to yourself and don't tell me.

392
00:34:45,237 --> 00:34:46,384
What are you talking about?

393
00:34:47,776 --> 00:34:48,776
Never mind.

394
00:34:51,702 --> 00:34:54,489
Let's just stop here.
Don't dig any further.

395
00:34:55,036 --> 00:34:57,227
Are you nuts? Did you forget all that?

396
00:34:57,503 --> 00:35:00,694
Back in the Joseon era,
they'd be drawn and quartered for this!

397
00:35:05,804 --> 00:35:08,230
My mom left for work. Come eat.

398
00:35:15,384 --> 00:35:16,760
What are you staring at?

399
00:35:17,257 --> 00:35:18,390
You're going to burn a hole in my face.

400
00:35:20,289 --> 00:35:21,784
I just can't get used to it.

401
00:35:24,757 --> 00:35:28,909
The world's full of all sorts of people
with all sorts of stories.

402
00:35:29,464 --> 00:35:30,464
Just eat.

403
00:35:30,617 --> 00:35:33,664
My mom went to all the trouble
of making food that's good for the brain.

404
00:35:36,763 --> 00:35:38,266
Why are you living a double life?

405
00:35:38,577 --> 00:35:41,195
You say you're not a spy,
so why are you even fooling Su Nam?

406
00:35:42,124 --> 00:35:44,916
If she knew her son
was such a famous photographer,

407
00:35:45,069 --> 00:35:47,221
I think she would be thrilled.

408
00:35:49,049 --> 00:35:50,916
She wouldn't faint from joy.

409
00:35:51,844 --> 00:35:55,090
She'd faint from shock
at the first syllable of "camera."

410
00:35:55,404 --> 00:35:56,404
Why?

411
00:35:57,021 --> 00:35:59,810
A photographer's a thousand times better
than a jobless bum, isn't it?

412
00:36:01,816 --> 00:36:05,434
My father was a photographer,

413
00:36:06,372 --> 00:36:10,926
and he was trying to photograph an orchid
on a cliff when he lost his footing...

414
00:36:13,902 --> 00:36:15,138
No way.

415
00:36:15,776 --> 00:36:19,577
He fell off a cliff
taking pictures and died?

416
00:36:23,196 --> 00:36:25,629
So whenever she sees me with a camera,

417
00:36:26,083 --> 00:36:29,546
she smashes it on the spot
and won't let me anywhere near one.

418
00:36:32,737 --> 00:36:34,624
So there was a backstory.

419
00:36:36,259 --> 00:36:37,537
Now I kind of get it.

420
00:36:37,844 --> 00:36:41,557
And you still want to take pictures.
DNA doesn't lie.

421
00:36:45,775 --> 00:36:50,233
But if you understand
other families so well,

422
00:36:50,627 --> 00:36:52,909
why can't you understand your own family?

423
00:36:53,317 --> 00:36:55,758
Did you call Gyu Seo to see if he's okay?

424
00:36:56,903 --> 00:36:59,198
He must be all better.
That guy is tough as nails.

425
00:37:00,563 --> 00:37:02,700
He's not a kid.
Why ask him every little thing?

426
00:37:03,724 --> 00:37:06,484
Gyu Seo told me not to tell you,
so I wasn't going to,

427
00:37:07,864 --> 00:37:11,245
but even if it's not a ruptured eardrum,

428
00:37:11,640 --> 00:37:13,877
he'll have some hearing problems
from now on.

429
00:37:14,497 --> 00:37:17,267
Gyu Seo, Gyu Rim, all of them.

430
00:37:17,269 --> 00:37:20,489
The only people who won't let go of you,
no matter what you do,

431
00:37:20,490 --> 00:37:21,962
are your family.

432
00:37:22,170 --> 00:37:25,350
You brat with less sense than
a sesame seed on seasoned spinach.

433
00:37:25,580 --> 00:37:28,389
What are you, a principal giving a speech?

434
00:37:28,677 --> 00:37:30,677
Why is your lecture so long?

435
00:37:31,030 --> 00:37:32,464
Let's just eat!

436
00:38:16,625 --> 00:38:20,253
(Gyeol's Homeroom Teacher)

437
00:38:25,561 --> 00:38:28,354
(Gyeol's Homeroom Teacher)

438
00:38:33,917 --> 00:38:36,904
Hello, Ms. Kwon. This is Gyeol's mom...

439
00:38:37,585 --> 00:38:39,439
Han Gyu O's sister.

440
00:38:39,809 --> 00:38:43,550
Could I see you for a moment
whenever you have time?

441
00:38:54,703 --> 00:38:56,552
Why are you taking so long to decide?

442
00:38:57,043 --> 00:39:00,210
Radish kimchi is radish kimchi,
and steamed eggs are steamed eggs.

443
00:39:00,598 --> 00:39:03,140
Hesitating like that...

444
00:39:03,165 --> 00:39:05,607
won't make what's already made
taste any better.

445
00:39:08,629 --> 00:39:10,029
When does the owner come in?

446
00:39:14,189 --> 00:39:15,617
How would I know?

447
00:39:16,298 --> 00:39:19,042
She might've gone on a delivery
and stopped somewhere on the way.

448
00:39:20,117 --> 00:39:23,417
Are you here to buy side dishes,
or to see the owner?

449
00:39:23,470 --> 00:39:26,241
She's already seeing someone, you know.

450
00:39:29,690 --> 00:39:31,348
I'm back.

451
00:39:31,373 --> 00:39:33,290
There's the boss.

452
00:39:42,003 --> 00:39:43,537
What are you doing here?

453
00:39:43,637 --> 00:39:45,493
I was worried and wanted
to see if you're okay.

454
00:39:47,351 --> 00:39:49,609
I texted you a week ago.

455
00:39:49,803 --> 00:39:53,612
That I went to the hospital right away,
and they said I'm fine, so don't worry.

456
00:39:55,103 --> 00:39:58,711
But how did you know this was my shop?

457
00:39:59,036 --> 00:40:01,292
A friend of mine is a regular here.

458
00:40:01,930 --> 00:40:06,501
My friend happens to share your name,
so I thought it was a funny coincidence.

459
00:40:07,315 --> 00:40:08,315
Excuse me a second.

460
00:40:10,168 --> 00:40:11,920
Side dishes.

461
00:40:15,437 --> 00:40:16,823
What are you doing?

462
00:40:17,004 --> 00:40:18,564
I'm going to send it to my friend.

463
00:40:18,664 --> 00:40:19,924
To show I've been to this shop too.

464
00:40:21,390 --> 00:40:23,684
I'm sorry, but please
delete that right now.

465
00:40:24,083 --> 00:40:25,283
Yes, of course.

466
00:40:26,264 --> 00:40:27,264
I'll delete it right away.

467
00:40:30,915 --> 00:40:32,330
Excuse me!

468
00:40:38,663 --> 00:40:40,796
I felt he was weird from the start.

469
00:40:41,222 --> 00:40:43,291
He wasn't buying anything,
just hanging around.

470
00:40:43,613 --> 00:40:44,613
Do you know him?

471
00:40:56,485 --> 00:40:58,558
(Han Gyu Rim)

472
00:41:04,825 --> 00:41:08,478
(Gyu Yeong)

473
00:41:09,189 --> 00:41:11,008
That's your sister, Han Gyu Rim, right?

474
00:41:11,517 --> 00:41:15,310
If you don't want your family to get hurt,
come out now, Han Gyu Yeong.

475
00:41:16,659 --> 00:41:19,136
This psycho, seriously!

476
00:41:24,063 --> 00:41:26,728
What should I do?
Should I call the police?

477
00:41:29,403 --> 00:41:31,421
No. Send them in.

478
00:41:34,463 --> 00:41:35,463
Yes.

479
00:41:39,390 --> 00:41:41,258
Okay, you can go now.

480
00:41:42,583 --> 00:41:44,356
(Chairman Jang Hun Tae)

481
00:41:54,516 --> 00:41:56,377
And what's this now?

482
00:41:56,743 --> 00:42:01,240
We're sorry. We weren't thinking.

483
00:42:02,890 --> 00:42:06,368
We dared to run our mouths off
at you, sir.

484
00:42:06,510 --> 00:42:08,875
We're deeply sorry.

485
00:42:10,197 --> 00:42:11,995
Forget the ten million dollars,

486
00:42:11,996 --> 00:42:15,077
just give us five million dollars,
like we first agreed...

487
00:42:15,078 --> 00:42:16,244
I told you before, didn't I?

488
00:42:17,157 --> 00:42:19,597
That I won't give you people
a single cent.

489
00:42:19,730 --> 00:42:20,864
We're sorry.

490
00:42:22,154 --> 00:42:24,059
I ran my mouth.

491
00:42:24,230 --> 00:42:28,455
We're sorry. We must've lost our minds.

492
00:42:28,628 --> 00:42:29,831
But what can I do?

493
00:42:30,525 --> 00:42:34,421
I'm not the type to easily reverse
a decision once I've made it.

494
00:42:37,383 --> 00:42:39,276
If you're done talking, you can leave.

495
00:42:39,550 --> 00:42:42,664
You're not even worth a glass of water,
so go.

496
00:42:42,941 --> 00:42:44,303
And...

497
00:42:45,447 --> 00:42:47,638
Don't barge into my office like this.

498
00:42:47,663 --> 00:42:52,237
If there's a problem,
go through my lawyers.

499
00:42:59,516 --> 00:43:01,264
About those lawyers.

500
00:43:01,371 --> 00:43:05,521
They're the best in the country
and very expensive.

501
00:43:06,140 --> 00:43:11,677
Why pay such enormous fees
over something like this?

502
00:43:11,966 --> 00:43:13,903
Settle with us instead.

503
00:43:13,937 --> 00:43:16,036
We'll make it worth your while.

504
00:43:16,061 --> 00:43:20,970
Forget five million. Just cut it in half.
Give us two and a half million.

505
00:43:21,276 --> 00:43:24,352
You know getting lawyers involved
will only spread more rumors, right?

506
00:43:24,650 --> 00:43:28,362
These days, rumors are scarier
than the truth.

507
00:43:29,100 --> 00:43:31,270
Are you going to let Gyu
Yeong's life be ruined?

508
00:43:32,269 --> 00:43:34,857
It's not just Gyu Yeong, sir.

509
00:43:35,412 --> 00:43:39,356
Above all, we can't let this
tarnish your reputation, can we?

510
00:43:39,381 --> 00:43:40,411
No.

511
00:43:40,436 --> 00:43:44,688
You're revered as
the Confucius of the business world.

512
00:43:44,713 --> 00:43:47,439
Your honor and dignity, sir.

513
00:43:47,464 --> 00:43:50,346
But I don't have any honor or dignity...

514
00:43:50,740 --> 00:43:53,386
that I'd protect
by scheming with you people.

515
00:43:54,036 --> 00:43:57,509
And even if I did, so what
if it gets a little dented?

516
00:43:59,097 --> 00:44:00,740
It's not like I can take
it with me when I die.

517
00:44:01,494 --> 00:44:02,494
Listen.

518
00:44:04,137 --> 00:44:06,626
Do you really think
threats like this still work?

519
00:44:08,504 --> 00:44:09,646
Listen carefully.

520
00:44:10,530 --> 00:44:12,707
I'm sure my lawyers told you,

521
00:44:13,506 --> 00:44:16,931
but I was the one
who pushed this marriage.

522
00:44:19,597 --> 00:44:23,554
I had no idea what lousy, scamming trash
you people were.

523
00:44:24,456 --> 00:44:26,761
I just wanted to marry
my daughter off well,

524
00:44:26,915 --> 00:44:30,782
and I got greedy and went too far.

525
00:44:31,690 --> 00:44:34,723
If I have to pay for that, I will.

526
00:44:34,947 --> 00:44:38,124
But from this moment on,

527
00:44:38,939 --> 00:44:41,942
if Gyu Yeong's name ever comes out
of your mouths again,

528
00:44:41,967 --> 00:44:46,772
I'll put my whole fortune on the line...

529
00:44:47,635 --> 00:44:50,742
and make you pay for it till the very end.

530
00:44:51,177 --> 00:44:53,267
- Sir.
- Sir.

531
00:44:53,616 --> 00:44:55,400
That's all I have to say.

532
00:44:55,746 --> 00:44:57,090
Sir.

533
00:44:59,761 --> 00:45:03,282
As a parent myself,
I really want to ask you something.

534
00:45:03,868 --> 00:45:08,853
Your son grew up learning from you,
so I can see why he turned out this way,

535
00:45:10,119 --> 00:45:11,538
but you're his parents.

536
00:45:12,214 --> 00:45:16,897
How could you risk your son's life
by pulling off such a ridiculous scam?

537
00:45:16,898 --> 00:45:18,863
How is that even possible?

538
00:45:19,550 --> 00:45:21,863
Even if money blinded you
to everything else,

539
00:45:22,011 --> 00:45:23,403
you're his parents!

540
00:45:25,183 --> 00:45:28,070
Even animals give their lives
to protect their young,

541
00:45:28,944 --> 00:45:30,357
and you're human beings!

542
00:45:32,158 --> 00:45:36,429
If you're human, you'd rip out your heart
to protect your child...

543
00:45:36,454 --> 00:45:40,774
and want to make them happy!
That's what parents and humans do!

544
00:45:46,245 --> 00:45:47,650
See you at the police station.

545
00:45:49,050 --> 00:45:50,236
Sir!

546
00:45:50,261 --> 00:45:51,976
(Damga Charcoal Grill)

547
00:45:51,978 --> 00:45:53,950
Here you are. Enjoy.

548
00:46:05,273 --> 00:46:10,603
My daughter's face is prettier
than any flower.

549
00:46:13,450 --> 00:46:18,503
Could you move the baby's breath
so I can see your face?

550
00:46:48,030 --> 00:46:50,258
Congratulations, Mom.

551
00:46:52,618 --> 00:46:53,804
Thank you.

552
00:46:56,430 --> 00:46:57,770
Thank you, sweetheart.

553
00:47:05,310 --> 00:47:07,061
Slow down. You'll get a stomachache.

554
00:47:07,996 --> 00:47:09,852
- The meat's so good.
- Yeah.

555
00:47:16,723 --> 00:47:19,674
Is there something you want to tell me?

556
00:47:24,016 --> 00:47:25,652
So there is something.

557
00:47:30,464 --> 00:47:32,096
I won't steal your food,

558
00:47:32,204 --> 00:47:36,329
so chew it well, swallow it all,
and eat slowly.

559
00:47:48,835 --> 00:47:50,241
This could be trouble.

560
00:47:51,037 --> 00:47:54,350
Once your tears start,
you can never stop them.

561
00:47:57,276 --> 00:48:00,001
If you have something to say,
tell me everything.

562
00:48:02,017 --> 00:48:04,163
Don't swallow it down with the meat.

563
00:48:23,077 --> 00:48:24,444
Mom, I...

564
00:48:26,683 --> 00:48:28,563
I met Han Gyu Rim.

565
00:48:30,849 --> 00:48:36,909
But how can she be so mature,
warm, and kind?

566
00:48:37,190 --> 00:48:38,870
It makes me feel so guilty.

567
00:48:42,230 --> 00:48:47,695
Is it because I cursed her, saying,
"Han Gyu Rim, don't you be happy either?"

568
00:48:49,210 --> 00:48:54,990
What do I do, Mom? I feel so bad.

569
00:48:56,743 --> 00:49:00,294
What on earth did I do to Han Gyu Rim?

570
00:49:07,063 --> 00:49:09,203
Her baby died.

571
00:49:12,896 --> 00:49:17,746
Seven years ago,
when she called you asking you to come,

572
00:49:18,121 --> 00:49:22,924
the baby she'd given birth to had died.

573
00:49:43,450 --> 00:49:45,283
- Ji Yeong.
- Yes, ma'am.

574
00:49:45,866 --> 00:49:48,723
- I'll be right back.
- Okay.

575
00:49:49,395 --> 00:49:56,395
(Suragan Side Dishes)

576
00:50:10,891 --> 00:50:12,149
What are you doing?

577
00:50:15,476 --> 00:50:16,843
Come here.

578
00:50:18,110 --> 00:50:19,503
Hurry.

579
00:50:24,343 --> 00:50:25,756
Don't mess with Gyu Rim.

580
00:50:26,336 --> 00:50:28,708
She's about to lose it because of Gyu O,

581
00:50:28,733 --> 00:50:33,892
and if she meets you too,
she'll overload and explode.

582
00:50:37,397 --> 00:50:41,704
She found out Gyu O's a gigolo.
No, that he used to be a gigolo.

583
00:50:43,530 --> 00:50:44,916
Gyu Rim found out.

584
00:50:46,545 --> 00:50:48,310
It's hot.

585
00:50:50,090 --> 00:50:51,663
So why did you come, anyway?

586
00:50:52,850 --> 00:50:55,096
Last time, you just tossed
her a lunch box and left.

587
00:50:57,476 --> 00:50:59,716
I should've taken them with me.

588
00:51:01,070 --> 00:51:02,070
What?

589
00:51:02,256 --> 00:51:04,203
Gyu Rim, Gyu Yeong, Gyu O...

590
00:51:05,989 --> 00:51:08,032
I shouldn't have left
them with you, Seok Jung.

591
00:51:09,127 --> 00:51:12,157
I should've raised them
myself, no matter what.

592
00:51:13,163 --> 00:51:16,629
Then my Gyu Rim...

593
00:51:18,669 --> 00:51:21,590
would've gone to college somehow,

594
00:51:22,531 --> 00:51:29,443
and I wouldn't have let her live
looked down on and disrespected like this.

595
00:51:29,963 --> 00:51:32,467
- Hey.
- And my Gyu O...

596
00:51:32,650 --> 00:51:36,309
If I'd raised him,
at least he wouldn't have become a gigolo.

597
00:51:37,070 --> 00:51:41,129
If I'd raised them,
they might not have been anything special,

598
00:51:41,723 --> 00:51:44,613
but at least they'd have lived
normal lives like everyone else...

599
00:51:44,638 --> 00:51:48,745
You think kids grow up
the way parents want?

600
00:51:48,770 --> 00:51:51,357
You think I wanted
to raise them like that?

601
00:51:51,844 --> 00:51:54,536
I was raising kids without a mom too...

602
00:51:54,561 --> 00:51:56,460
This is all because of you.

603
00:51:56,916 --> 00:51:59,930
You fell for another
woman and kicked me out.

604
00:52:01,022 --> 00:52:03,116
So why am I the one to blame?

605
00:52:03,384 --> 00:52:05,465
You did everything wrong,

606
00:52:05,490 --> 00:52:10,326
so why was I torn apart from my children,
unable to see them though I missed them,

607
00:52:11,856 --> 00:52:15,890
and why am I the only one
who has to be the villain? Why?

608
00:52:17,811 --> 00:52:21,424
Is this right? Is this fair?

609
00:52:22,017 --> 00:52:23,967
You're the one who's trash,

610
00:52:24,374 --> 00:52:26,849
so why does it have to be
this unfair? Why?

611
00:52:27,596 --> 00:52:30,907
Hey, when did I ever stop
you from seeing them?

612
00:52:31,003 --> 00:52:35,834
You're the one who cut off contact
and never called once in 17 years.

613
00:52:35,859 --> 00:52:37,466
Because I didn't know!

614
00:52:37,896 --> 00:52:43,192
I didn't know the girl you were nuts about
abandoned the kids and ran off!

615
00:52:44,284 --> 00:52:47,433
Since it had come to that,
I wanted them to forget their mom...

616
00:52:48,407 --> 00:52:51,089
and get attached to their stepmom.

617
00:52:51,717 --> 00:52:57,213
I didn't want them to be confused.
I didn't want it to be harder on them.

618
00:52:58,090 --> 00:53:02,157
Really? That was your big, deep plan?

619
00:53:03,990 --> 00:53:07,369
You remarried a rich tycoon
and started a new family,

620
00:53:07,397 --> 00:53:09,537
so I thought you'd forgotten
all about the kids.

621
00:53:09,538 --> 00:53:12,364
How could I forget?

622
00:53:12,389 --> 00:53:15,362
How could I forget my own children?

623
00:53:22,183 --> 00:53:24,422
But why did I do that?

624
00:53:25,890 --> 00:53:28,476
Why didn't I go see Gyu Rim?

625
00:53:29,949 --> 00:53:33,678
She wanted so badly to see me.
Why did I do that?

626
00:53:35,293 --> 00:53:39,056
Am I out of my mind? Am I even human?

627
00:53:41,250 --> 00:53:44,650
I said things I didn't mean
to Gyu Yeong and Gyu O too.

628
00:53:44,976 --> 00:53:47,273
Why on earth did I do that?

629
00:53:48,543 --> 00:53:50,210
I must be crazy.

630
00:53:51,324 --> 00:53:55,450
I must be out of my mind.
I must really be out of my mind.

631
00:54:02,583 --> 00:54:04,137
I'm really sorry I drove you crazy.

632
00:54:04,290 --> 00:54:06,737
I wasn't in my right mind
back then either,

633
00:54:07,413 --> 00:54:09,960
and I'm really sorry
I drove you crazy too.

634
00:54:10,930 --> 00:54:14,570
Now that you point it all out one by one,

635
00:54:16,190 --> 00:54:20,196
I can see just how much I've done wrong.

636
00:54:21,536 --> 00:54:24,803
Why did I do that? Am I even human?

637
00:54:47,609 --> 00:54:49,483
Please punish me.

638
00:54:51,803 --> 00:54:54,816
Punish me for leaving my children behind.

639
00:54:57,010 --> 00:54:58,710
Please punish me.

640
00:55:00,375 --> 00:55:02,302
This is the model I mentioned last time.

641
00:55:02,503 --> 00:55:04,596
He's got a great look, so people love him.

642
00:55:05,817 --> 00:55:08,663
This is how the photo
shoot went this time.

643
00:55:09,857 --> 00:55:11,710
The internal preview
got great reactions too.

644
00:55:12,323 --> 00:55:18,867
I did it. To my son, Mu Jin.

645
00:55:19,642 --> 00:55:23,540
To ruin him completely, I...

646
00:55:24,220 --> 00:55:28,183
I paid those people to do it all. So what?

647
00:55:28,768 --> 00:55:30,315
You...

648
00:55:31,110 --> 00:55:35,577
To make you give up even a second sooner.

649
00:55:37,018 --> 00:55:38,211
Ma'am?

650
00:55:39,464 --> 00:55:44,909
This is bad. I remember now. What do I do?

651
00:55:45,730 --> 00:55:51,732
I called Han Gyu Rim drunk
and confessed everything.

652
00:55:52,127 --> 00:55:54,209
What do I do?

653
00:55:56,084 --> 00:55:57,377
What do I do?

654
00:55:57,683 --> 00:56:02,050
That girl must've told him everything,

655
00:56:02,089 --> 00:56:05,449
and Mu Jin must've foamed at the mouth
and keeled over.

656
00:56:05,562 --> 00:56:08,443
He'll say he'll never see me
again until he dies. What do I do?

657
00:56:08,896 --> 00:56:11,948
Didn't you think he'd cut ties with you
when you did all that?

658
00:56:11,973 --> 00:56:16,577
How can a girl have such a big mouth?

659
00:56:16,602 --> 00:56:21,157
What's she thinking, telling on me
for something I said drunk?

660
00:56:21,587 --> 00:56:24,435
Hey, if I take a girl like that
as my daughter-in-law,

661
00:56:24,437 --> 00:56:27,650
there'll be an all-out in-law war,
you know that?

662
00:56:28,902 --> 00:56:30,479
Don't worry too much.

663
00:56:30,504 --> 00:56:32,957
She wouldn't have said a word to Mu Jin.

664
00:56:33,397 --> 00:56:36,169
Han Gyu Rim is much more thoughtful
than you think, Mom.

665
00:56:37,710 --> 00:56:40,440
What do I do?

666
00:56:47,157 --> 00:56:50,263
Yes, the Chairwoman isn't in any condition
to see anyone right now...

667
00:56:50,288 --> 00:56:51,741
It's Jeong Woo, ma'am.

668
00:57:01,116 --> 00:57:03,650
Jeong Woo, it's been so long.

669
00:57:05,576 --> 00:57:07,856
What brings you here?

670
00:57:10,750 --> 00:57:13,614
Sit down. Let's sit first.

671
00:57:51,437 --> 00:57:52,637
Hello.

672
00:58:25,183 --> 00:58:26,443
Go ahead.

673
00:58:28,424 --> 00:58:32,363
Do you know you haven't said
a word this whole time?

674
00:58:35,890 --> 00:58:40,465
You can curse me or blame me,

675
00:58:41,546 --> 00:58:43,263
so please say something. Anything.

676
00:58:51,356 --> 00:58:52,616
I'm sorry.

677
00:58:55,810 --> 00:58:58,357
Don't say sorry. Curse me.

678
00:58:58,744 --> 00:59:01,510
I'm the one who should be sorry, not you.

679
00:59:10,195 --> 00:59:11,562
I'm sorry.

680
00:59:14,150 --> 00:59:16,616
I told the principal everything today.

681
00:59:17,357 --> 00:59:19,877
That I don't know any Han Gyu O.

682
00:59:20,743 --> 00:59:22,557
That I'd never heard that name before.

683
00:59:27,243 --> 00:59:31,728
That the woman who came to the school
mistook me for someone else,

684
00:59:32,466 --> 00:59:34,609
and that whoever posted
online to frame me,

685
00:59:34,804 --> 00:59:37,682
whoever wrote fake comments,
whoever made fake news shorts,

686
00:59:37,731 --> 00:59:40,858
I'd track them all down, press charges,
and come down hard on them.

687
00:59:42,732 --> 00:59:43,837
So...

688
00:59:46,506 --> 00:59:47,870
Please help me.

689
00:59:51,890 --> 00:59:55,310
Help me keep my job
and stay at the school,

690
00:59:57,536 --> 01:00:02,304
so I can keep earning money
and take care of my family.

691
01:00:03,799 --> 01:00:05,270
Please help me.

692
01:00:10,976 --> 01:00:13,489
People can change their minds.

693
01:00:15,463 --> 01:00:20,445
I lived recklessly, not knowing better,
but when I faced reality,

694
01:00:22,108 --> 01:00:24,197
I could come to my senses.

695
01:00:35,783 --> 01:00:36,950
Of course.

696
01:00:39,036 --> 01:00:40,422
That can happen.

697
01:00:41,969 --> 01:00:44,656
It can absolutely happen, Ms. Kwon.

698
01:00:46,690 --> 01:00:49,292
I didn't come here to curse you,

699
01:00:50,574 --> 01:00:52,952
and I didn't come to blame you either.

700
01:00:54,611 --> 01:00:58,560
I just wanted to thank you...

701
01:01:01,528 --> 01:01:08,213
for caring so much
about Gyu O all this time,

702
01:01:11,203 --> 01:01:17,103
and to tell you to take care of yourself
and never skip a meal.

703
01:01:17,943 --> 01:01:20,049
That's what I came to say.

704
01:01:25,223 --> 01:01:26,456
Thank you.

705
01:01:30,710 --> 01:01:34,748
For loving Gyu O.

706
01:01:36,483 --> 01:01:39,563
Thank you so much, Ms. Kwon.

707
01:02:12,277 --> 01:02:13,383
Han Gyu O.

708
01:02:23,569 --> 01:02:25,089
Why aren't you going inside?

709
01:02:27,191 --> 01:02:28,377
No reason.

710
01:02:29,916 --> 01:02:33,656
The breeze is nice. You go in first.

711
01:02:49,177 --> 01:02:51,950
Gyu O, if it hurts...

712
01:02:54,737 --> 01:02:56,230
scream.

713
01:03:00,190 --> 01:03:02,170
Don't pretend it doesn't hurt.

714
01:03:04,330 --> 01:03:06,096
Don't pretend you're fine.

715
01:03:08,703 --> 01:03:12,663
Say it's killing you. Beg for help.

716
01:03:15,104 --> 01:03:16,377
Scream.

717
01:03:20,256 --> 01:03:25,245
If it's hard, say it's hard.
If you're lonely, say you're lonely.

718
01:03:26,324 --> 01:03:29,529
Yell it out, Gyu O.

719
01:03:36,581 --> 01:03:38,083
This drives me nuts.

720
01:03:39,430 --> 01:03:41,176
This drives me nuts!

721
01:03:43,223 --> 01:03:47,375
If it weren't for you,
I could've lived however I wanted.

722
01:03:48,949 --> 01:03:51,771
I could've broken anyone
I wanted to break,

723
01:03:51,899 --> 01:03:54,663
killed anyone I wanted to kill,

724
01:03:55,629 --> 01:03:59,701
and even if I went to prison,
I could've followed my heart...

725
01:04:01,010 --> 01:04:03,684
and at least lived
with some peace of mind...

726
01:04:09,869 --> 01:04:11,955
It drives me nuts. Seriously.

727
01:04:18,597 --> 01:04:21,916
Gyu Rim, can't we just cut ties?

728
01:04:22,984 --> 01:04:25,557
Can't we be strangers, like Han Gyu Yeong?

729
01:04:26,556 --> 01:04:28,889
You're driving me crazy!

730
01:04:28,914 --> 01:04:31,567
I'm losing my mind! You know that?

731
01:04:39,669 --> 01:04:41,596
I'll never cut ties with you.

732
01:04:42,150 --> 01:04:46,696
No matter what you say to me,
I won't cut ties with you.

733
01:04:48,264 --> 01:04:50,350
Gyu Yeong is the only one
I've cut ties with, and that's enough.

734
01:04:52,896 --> 01:04:55,889
I'll stick to you like glue
till the end...

735
01:04:56,084 --> 01:04:58,250
and cling to your legs.

736
01:04:59,177 --> 01:05:01,179
If you throw me in the trash,

737
01:05:01,260 --> 01:05:03,803
I'll crawl right out of it.

738
01:05:04,916 --> 01:05:08,001
Even if you go crazy,
even if you lose your mind,

739
01:05:08,523 --> 01:05:12,130
I'll grab you by the collar
and follow you till the day I die.

740
01:05:13,970 --> 01:05:17,446
Got it? You brat.

741
01:05:53,840 --> 01:05:55,993
(Love on the Menu)

742
01:05:56,018 --> 01:05:59,468
The guy who did that to my mom
can't get to be shamelessly happy.

743
01:05:59,493 --> 01:06:01,201
I thought it was love, but it's not.

744
01:06:01,226 --> 01:06:04,201
You little brat! How dare you
lay a hand on someone so precious?

745
01:06:04,226 --> 01:06:06,313
You think I did it just for me?

746
01:06:06,371 --> 01:06:08,691
What did she say was the reason
she did something so absurd?

747
01:06:08,716 --> 01:06:11,850
Have you seen anyone strange
coming in and out of the side dish shop?

748
01:06:11,875 --> 01:06:13,048
You know Han Gyu Yeong, right?

749
01:06:13,623 --> 01:06:17,502
That bastard's a total psycho,
so run right now, Han Gyu Rim!

750
01:06:18,903 --> 01:06:20,703
Dramaday.me
